<title>INDIA: Indian gold falls, silver ends steady.</title>
<headline>Indian gold falls, silver ends steady.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian gold prices closer lower on improved supply on Friday after a steady opening, dealers said.</p>
<p>It was down five rupees per 10 grammes on Thursday.</p>
<p>Prices of a gold biscuit (116.50 grammes) fell by 50 rupees at 60,500 rupees. It was down by 100 rupees on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;Demand for yesterday's festival is over and fresh seasonal buying will be seen only next week,&quot; one dealer said.</p>
<p>Silver on the other hand remained steady throughout on thin activity. &quot;Most of the business was reported in gold only while silver was neglected,&quot; one broker said.  </p>
